            <title>[LU-20689] lfs setquota: support decimal (SI) size suffixes for block and inode limits</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20689</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;1) Support decimal (SI) size suffixes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every KMGTPE suffix is a power of two today, so "1G", "1GiB" and "1GB" all mean 1073741824. There is no way to enter a limit in the decimal units that capacity documents are written in, and a value copied from one is over-provisioned by 7.4% at GB and 10% at TB. A trailing "B" should select decimal units:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
1G, 1GiB  -&amp;gt;  2^30   (unchanged)
1GB      -&amp;gt;  10^9&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2) Reject anything that is not a standard spelling.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only the first character after the suffix is checked, so "1Gjunk" and "1Gi" are silently accepted as 1 GiB.  Accept exactly "1G", "1GB" and "1GiB", in either case, and reject the rest.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
